Z||000000||mope||01-04-2001||11:43 PM||||can someone please list the diffrences between the 85 gt and a 86 se that has a 6 cylinder?<BR>I'm debating between the two.<BR>thanks<P>m0pe||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-05-2001||12:12 AM||||They are absolutely identical.  The only difference is late '86 SE's came with the Getrag 5-sp.<P>GM renamed the '85 GT in '86 to SE since they had the fastback GT coming out.  They sold a TON of '86 SE's for most of the year, since the fastback wasn't ready until March '86.  The SE continued into '87, but they only sold a fraction of what they did in '86 since there was no waiting for the fastback. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Raydar||01-05-2001||12:16 AM||||The 85 GT had gray ground F/X. The 86 SE had black ones. The 86 SE also had the center console gauges, and backlighted main gauges.<BR>The 85 had "reflector" lighted gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-05-2001||01:18 AM||||OK......let me rephrase that.......they are physically identical, but have a few minor cosmetic differences.||||reg||10
Z||000004||mope||01-05-2001||01:20 AM||||isnt the steering wheel diffrent? like has thos side buttins for the horn?<P>m0pe<P>thanks for the help||||reg||5
Z||000005||mrfiero||01-05-2001||01:43 AM||||That would be one of the cosmetic differences.   For all intents and purposes they are the same car.  Neither is really above each other.....I would buy a nice '86 SE over a ratty '85 GT and vice versa.  The minor cosmetic differences don't mean much when you come down to it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||01-05-2001||02:49 AM||||Also the logo's and washer fluid tank!<P>There are some little subtle difference, but very little. If you put GT badges on an SE, few people could tell the differece.||||reg||1
